Usages:
  registration_state_derivation: |
    Registration/account state is derived, not stored directly: raw flags (reregistration
    in progress, transfer in progress, deregistered/delinked, primary vs linked device) are
    persisted independently, then combined into a single `TSRegistrationState` case on read.
    Any code that changes one of the underlying flags must re-derive and cache the combined
    state rather than assume it can be read back verbatim.
  transaction_scoped_access: |
    All reads and writes of local account/registration state take an explicit read or write
    transaction token parameter; there is no ambient/global mutable state accessed without
    a transaction.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the single authoritative source of truth for the local device's registration
  and account identity: local ACI/PNI/phone number, device id, server auth token, registration
  id per identity, manual-message-fetch flag, and phone-number discoverability.
  Use `registration_state_derivation` when implementing any state-transition method.
  Use `transaction_scoped_access` for every read/write method on this cell's types.

---

"TSAccountManager()":
  location: TSAccountManager.swift
  annotations: |
    Protocol defining read access to local account/registration state, plus two narrow
    mutation-capability protocols intended only for the small set of collaborators allowed to
    change identity/registration state directly.

    Use `registration_state_derivation` for the registration-state accessor below.
    Use `transaction_scoped_access` for all methods below.
  methods:
    "localIdentifiers(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> identifiers: LocalIdentifiers?": |
      Returns the local user's ACI/PNI/phone-number identifiers, or nil if not yet registered.
    "registrationState(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> state: TSRegistrationState": |
      Derives and returns the combined registration lifecycle state.

      Algorithm:
      1. Read the raw persisted flags (reregistering/relinking/deregistered/delinked/transferring).
      2. Combine them into exactly one `TSRegistrationState` case per `registration_state_derivation`.
    "registrationDate(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> date: Date?": |
      Returns the timestamp the device most recently completed registration, if any.
    "storedDeviceId(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> deviceId: LocalDeviceId": |
      Returns the locally stored device id, either a concrete valid id or an invalid marker.
    "setRegistrationId(newRegistrationId: Int, identity: String, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Persists a new Signal Protocol registration id for the given identity.

      `identity`: which of the two identity keys (ACI/PNI) this registration id belongs to
    "getRegistrationId(identity: String, tx: DBReadTransaction) -> registrationId: Int?": |
      Reads back the previously stored registration id for the given identity, if any.
    "isManualMessageFetchEnabled(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> isEnabled: Bool": |
      Returns whether the device is configured to fetch messages manually (rather than via push).
    "setIsManualMessageFetchEnabled(isEnabled: Bool, tx: DBWriteTransaction)": |
      Persists the manual-message-fetch preference.
    "phoneNumberDiscoverability(tx: DBReadTransaction) -> discoverability: String?": |
      Returns whether the local phone number is currently discoverable by others, if known.

"TSRegistrationState()":
  location: TSRegistrationState.swift
  annotations: |
    Pure value type enumerating the finite set of local device lifecycle states: unregistered,
    reregistering, relinking, registered, provisioned, deregistered, delinked, and the three
    transfer-in-progress variants (incoming, primary outgoing, linked outgoing) plus transferred.

    Use `registration_state_derivation` — this type is the output of that derivation, never
    constructed from raw flags by any caller other than `TSAccountManager`.
  properties:
    "isRegistered -> Bool": |
      True for the registered and provisioned cases.
    "wasEverRegistered -> Bool": |
      True for every case except unregistered.
    "isDeregistered -> Bool": |
      True for the deregistered and delinked cases.
    "isRegisteredPrimaryDevice -> Bool": |
      True when registered and the device is the account's primary device (not a linked device).

"RegistrationIdGenerator()":
  location: RegistrationIdGenerator.swift
  annotations: |
    Generates new Signal Protocol registration ids for use when registering an identity.
  methods:
    "generate() -> registrationId: Int": |
      Returns a new random registration id in the valid Signal Protocol range.

